within Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.J_AntiinfectivesForSystemicUse.J01F_MacrolidesLincosamidesAndStreptogramins.J01FA10_Azithromycin;
model Azithromycin_Hao2013_PD_pcs
  "indirect_response_i exposure-response sweep — Hao_2013 :: PCs (plasma proinflammatory cytokines)"
  extends Pharmacolibrary.Interfaces.PartialExposureResponseSweep(
    E0 = 4.98e-08,      // [kg/m3; pg·ml−1 × 1e-09]
    Emax = 0.83,  // type I effect term
    EC50 = 0.0063,  // [kg/m3; ug/ml × 0.001]
    gamma = 1,
    exposure_per_s = 0.001);   // 1 ug/ml per second
equation
  response = E0*(1 - Emax*frac);   // steady state, indirect response type I
  // defaulted: gamma
  annotation(experiment(StartTime = 0, StopTime = 63, Interval = 0.126),
    Documentation(info = "<html><body><h4>Azithromycin_Hao2013_PD_pcs</h4><p>The steady-state exposure-response curve of Hao K et al., <i>PloS one 8(1):e54981</i> 2013 (<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0054981\">doi:10.1371/journal.pone.0054981</a>) — plasma proinflammatory cytokines [pg·ml−1] against azithromycin ug/ml — obtained by sweeping the driver instead of simulating a dose. Model family: indirect_response_i.</p><h4>The parameters, in the paper's terms</h4><pre>  E0    =       49.8 pg·ml−1  drug-free response (baseline) (PCs,0, Q324)
  Emax  =       0.83          maximal effect term (Imax, Q323)
  EC50  =        6.3 ug/ml    exposure at half of the maximal effect term (IC50, Q322)
  gamma = (library default) Hill coefficient</pre><p>The algebra is <code>response = E0*(1 - Emax*frac)</code>; this model only supplies the numbers. The x axis is one ug/ml of azithromycin per second of simulated time (exposure is in kg/m3): there is no state, no dose and no kinetics — plot <code>response</code> against <code>exposure</code> (or <code>time</code>).</p><h4>What it reproduces</h4><pre>  exposure = 0         response 4.98e-08   (drug-free)
  exposure = EC50 (6.3 ug/ml)  response 2.913e-08
  exposure -> infinity  response 8.466e-09</pre></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from Hao_2013: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: accepted with caveats</li></ul></body></html>"));
end Azithromycin_Hao2013_PD_pcs;
